The vmstat command in Linux is used to report virtual memory statistics, but in practice it gives a high-level view of system performance including CPU, memory, swap, disk I/O, and process activity.

=======================================
🔹 Basic Syntax
=======================================
#vmstat [options] [delay] [count]


example: vmstat 1 5
➡ Updates every 1 second, 5 times


