=====================================================================================================================
🔹 Column-by-Column Explanation
=====================================================================================================================
=======================================
🧵 Procs
=======================================
| Column | Meaning                              |
| ------ | ------------------------------------ |
| `r`    | Runnable processes (waiting for CPU) |
| `b`    | Blocked processes (waiting for I/O)  |

👉 High r → CPU bottleneck
👉 High b → Disk / I/O issue


=======================================
🧠 Memory
=======================================
| Column  | Meaning                 |
| ------- | ----------------------- |
| `swpd`  | Used swap (KB)          |
| `free`  | Free memory             |
| `buff`  | Memory used for buffers |
| `cache` | Memory used for cache   |

👉 Linux uses free memory as cache (this is normal)

  
=======================================
🔁 Swap
=======================================
| Column | Meaning                   |
| ------ | ------------------------- |
| `si`   | Swap in (from disk → RAM) |
| `so`   | Swap out (RAM → disk)     |

👉 Non-zero si/so consistently = memory pressure
  
=======================================
💽 I/O
=======================================
| Column | Meaning                   |
| ------ | ------------------------- |
| `bi`   | Blocks received from disk |
| `bo`   | Blocks sent to disk       |

👉 High values → heavy disk activity

=======================================
⚙️ System
=======================================

| Column | Meaning                     |
| ------ | --------------------------- |
| `in`   | Interrupts per second       |
| `cs`   | Context switches per second |

👉 Very high cs → too many threads / processes
=======================================
🖥️ CPU
=======================================

| Column | Meaning              |
| ------ | -------------------- |
| `us`   | User CPU time        |
| `sy`   | System (kernel) time |
| `id`   | Idle CPU             |
| `wa`   | I/O wait             |
| `st`   | Steal time (VMs)     |

👉 High wa → disk latency
👉 High st → hypervisor over-commit (VM issue)



=======================================
Live monitoring
=======================================
vmstat 1

=======================================
Show memory in MB
=======================================
vmstat -S M

=======================================
Disk statistics
=======================================
vmstat -d






  
